{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.validation.criterion_trait`\n\n`Criterion::source_node_id` identifies the criterion's\n{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.validation.source_node`:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    // ...\n\n    /// The node this question is about.\n    fn source_node_id(&self) -> D::NodeId;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has one obligation. `Criterion::source_node_id` returns the criterion's source node as `D::NodeId`. The trait signature itself is only declared; the checkable behaviour is that a criterion's reported source node is the node it is evaluated on and that the validator uses it.\n\nTwo marked tests cover this:\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` uses the test `Review` criterion. Its `source_node_id` returns the descriptor's `source` field. The test runs `validator.verify(descriptor())` and asserts `value.source_node_id() == &Node(1)`. That shows the node the criterion reports is the node attached to the answer. The `Validator::verify` and `load_evidence` implementations take `criterion.source_node_id()` as the node. The test then stores the answer and reloads it through `load_evidence`. It asserts the loaded `source_node_id` equals the original, so the same node identity is used for persistence and lookup.\n- `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[review_graph_persists_and_reuses_a_negative_validation_through_the_sdk]` asserts `review().source_node_id() == node` directly on a real SDK criterion. It then checks that evidence for that node and criterion path is loaded, persisted and reused.\n\nBetween them, one test checks the trait method's return value directly and the other checks that the validator uses the value for execution and storage. I found no unacknowledged gap. The criterion-path and revision members are covered by other requirements, and the cited parent `criterion_trait` is context only.",
  "references": "2a0fb05f8fd461148265de0b6e203fb914e7ed9c75f88244f8ccf6a97b30f907",
